    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green (`AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are support classes). The full suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n**Format**: `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 LAST3 is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, NNNN is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count (e.g. `SMI-0007`).\n\nChanges:\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter.\n2. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** (new function) \u2014 reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, counts existing owners via `OwnerRepository.findAll().size()`, and sets `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, count + 1)`.\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `customerCode` step into the pipeline between `build` and `save` (under the same `transaction` governance), so the owner isn't yet counted when its sequence is computed \u2014 giving a clean per-owner increment.\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema so MapStruct maps it into the GET response DTO by name.\n5. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `customer_code` column. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is what makes the column exist there.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (verifying the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and the global sequence incrementing by one between consecutive creates) passes, and the full suite is green.",
